  "chapter": {
    "number": 73,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(74) A Psalm of",
          {
            "noteId": 132
          },
          "instruction for Asaph."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore have you rejected us, O God, for ever? therefore is your wrath kindled against the sheep of your pasture?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Remember your congregation which you have purchased from the beginning; you did ransom the rod of your inheritance; this mount Sion wherein you have lived.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Lift up your hands against their pride continually; because of all that the enemy has done wickedly in your holy places.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they that hate you have boasted in the midst of your feast; they have set up their standards for signs,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "ignorantly as it were in the entrance above;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "they cut down its doors at once with axes as in a wood of trees; they have broken it down with hatchet and stone cutter.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have burnt your sanctuary with fire to the ground; they have profaned the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 133
          },
          {
            "text": "habitation of your name.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have said in their heart, even all their kindred together, Come, let us abolish the feasts of the Lord from the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "We have not seen our signs; there is no longer a prophet; and God will not know us any more.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How long, O God, shall the enemy reproach? shall the enemy provoke your name forever?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore turn you away your hand, and your right hand from the midst of your bosom for ever?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But God is our King",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 134
          },
          {
            "text": "of old; he has wrought salvation in the midst of the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You did establish the sea, in your might, you did break to pieces the heads of the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 135
          },
          {
            "text": "dragons in the water.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You did break to pieces the heads of the dragon; you did give him for meat to the Ethiopian nations.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You did cleave fountains and torrents; you dried up",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 136
          },
          {
            "text": "mighty rivers.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The day is yours, and the night is yours; you have prepared the sun and the moon.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have made all the borders of the earth; you have made summer and spring.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Remember this your creation: an enemy has reproached the Lord, and a foolish people has provoked your name.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver not to the wild beasts a soul that gives praise to you: forget not for ever the souls of your poor.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Look upon your covenant: for the dark places of the earth are filled with the habitations of iniquity.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "let not the afflicted and shamed one be rejected: the poor and needy shall praise your name.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Arise, O God, plead your cause: remember your reproaches that come from the foolish one all the day.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Forget not the voice of your suppliants: let the pride of them that hate you continually ascend before you.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 132,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. understanding.",
        "reference": {
